dence":["Plan: 'The existing graph unit/interface suites are the behavioral oracle ... under tests/unit + tests/interfaces'","grep tests/unit for _find_direct_blockers / detect_newly_unblocked -> (no matches); grep tests/interfaces for _find_direct_blockers -> (no matches)","Actual coverage: tests/scripts/graph/test_graph_cycles.py:193,279 (check_cycle_at_level, _get_all_blocked_by); tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py:159 (detect_newly_unblocked)"],"finding":"The plan names its behavioral-oracle test suites as living 'under tests/unit + tests/interfaces', but the actual tests exercising all four refactored functions live under tests/scripts/graph/ (test_graph_cycles.py covers check_cycle_at_level and _get_all_blocked_by) and tests/scripts/ (test_ticket_unblock.py covers detect_newly_unblocked). tests/unit and tests/interfaces contain no matches for _find_direct_blockers, detect_newly_unblocked, or graph._unblock, so the named suites are not the behavior-preserving oracle the plan relies on.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc696a4dd5c95035e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Verification section ('under tests/unit + tests/interfaces') and Acceptance Criteria lines 3-4","norm_id":"n018c8d6b93d3d7bc","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["Executor runs the named tests/unit + tests/interfaces suites to confirm behavior parity and finds no relevant coverage, leaving the refactor un-validated by the stated oracle."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Replace the 'under tests/unit + tests/interfaces' phrasing with the concrete oracle paths: tests/scripts/graph/test_graph_cycles.py (cycle detection / _get_all_blocked_by) and tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py (detect_newly_unblocked), plus whatever suite covers _find_direct_blockers.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm (or add) that at least one existing graph test exercises a `blocks`/`depends_on` target with no backing ticket file, so the `_get_all_blocked_by` unconditional-add parity is genuinely proven by the oracle; otherwise add a RED-anchored fixture for that edge.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T6","T9"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Node-set parity for the two raw-reduce BFS functions is explicit: they still add every blocks/depends_on target unconditionally'","'verified by the existing graph cycle/blocker suites passing with no edits' — relies on inherited coverage of the nonexistent-target edge without confirming such a fixture exists"],"finding":"The plan designates the existing graph suites as the sole behavioral oracle for a subtle parity property (`_get_all_blocked_by`'s unconditional `blocked.add(target)` for targets that do not exist as nodes), but does not confirm any existing test actually exercises that specific edge case; if no test covers a `blocks`/`depends_on` target with no corresponding ticket file, a regression in the refactored `neighbors_fn` would pass green.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd2540a6ac7e466aa","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Verification / AC3","norm_id":"ne879e5e92308703b","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["The refactored bfs neighbors_fn accidentally filters out targets whose ticket file is missing, but every existing test only references existing targets, so the suite stays green despite a behavior change."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the pure `bfs` reconciles the divergent outputs: _get_all_blocked_by returns an ACCUMULATOR set (`blocked`) distinct from the visited set — it includes unconditionally-added targets (even nonexistent ids) and excludes the seed unless a real edge targets it — while check_cycle_at_level needs a bool (or `source_id in bfs(...)`); confirm the bfs contract (e.g. neighbors_fn contributes to an accumulator, and the returned set is the accumulator, not `visited`) so both functions' results are byte-identical to origin/main.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'add a PURE bfs(starts, neighbors_fn) -> set[str] skeleton (visited/queue only; no filtering policy)'","_graph.py:151 `blocked.add(target)` runs before existence checks, so returned `blocked` ≠ `visited` and may contain non-node ids","_get_all_blocked_by returns `blocked` (line 182), a set seeded-node-excluding and target-including — a `visited`-returning bfs would differ","check_cycle_at_level returns bool via `if current == source_id: return True` (line 244), not a set","check_would_create_cycle relies on `target_id in _get_all_blocked_by(source_id)` — spurious inclusion of the start node would change cycle results"],"finding":"The pure `bfs(starts, neighbors_fn) -> set[str]` skeleton is under-specified for the two target functions, which return structurally different results: `_get_all_blocked_by` returns its `blocked` set (which is NOT the visited set — `_graph.py:151` adds every blocks-target to `blocked` before any existence check, so it can include nonexistent ids never dequeued, and the seed `ticket_id` is in `visited` but not in `blocked`), while `check_cycle_at_level` returns a bool via a mid-loop early return. A generic bfs returning the visited set cannot reproduce `blocked`; and if it returned `visited` (which contains the start node) it would change `check_would_create_cycle`'s membership test (`target_id in _get_all_blocked_by(source_id)`).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc1daab2f01e65730","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 (graph/_relations.py bfs helper) / _graph.py:127-182, 223-276","norm_id":"ndd65663373d6f416","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["An edge whose depends_on/blocks target is a nonexistent ticket id (must still appear in _get_all_blocked_by's result)","A cycle-detection call where the queried node would be spuriously included if bfs returns visited"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Define bfs so the returned set is an accumulator fed by neighbors_fn (each discovered neighbor id added regardless of whether it is later visited/exists), NOT the visited set — matching _get_all_blocked_by's `blocked`; for check_cycle_at_level compute the full reachable set and test `source_id in result` (order-independent, so the mid-loop early return is safely equivalent).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severit